<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">14 May in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">9 events that happened on 14 May, from 1027 to 1973.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/reims" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/reims.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1027 CE <span class="tih-ago">999 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Robert II's son Henry is consecrated junior king at Reims</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/robert-ii-of-france">Robert II of France</a> had his second son, Henry, consecrated as junior king at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/reims">Reims</a> Cathedral, over the opposition of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prince-henry-the-navigator">Henry</a>'s mother Constance, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishops</a> and many princes. Hugh, the eldest son and first junior king, had died in 1025.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/robert-ii-of-france">Robert II of France</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1264">1264 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">762 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Simon de Montfort defeats Henry III at the Battle of Lewes</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">In the Second Barons' War, barons led by Simon de Montfort defeated King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-iii-of-england">Henry III of England</a> at Lewes in Sussex. The king was forced to sign the Mise of Lewes, ceding many of his powers to de Montfort.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/simon-de-montfort-6th-earl-of-leicester">Simon de Montfort</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-iii-of-england">Henry III of England</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1450">1450 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">576 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Sultan Murad II begins the siege of Krujë</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">An Ottoman army led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sultan">Sultan</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/murad-ii">Murad II</a> and his crown prince <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mehmed-ii">Mehmed II</a> besieged <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kruje">Krujë</a>, the Albanian capital of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/skanderbeg">Skanderbeg</a>'s <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/league-of-lezhe">League of Lezhë</a>. Harassed by Skanderbeg and weakened by disease, the Ottoman army eventually lifted the siege.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottoman Empire</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1607">1607 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">419 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">English colonists land at Jamestown</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Settlers of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/virginia">Virginia</a> Company came ashore on a peninsula in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/james-river">James River</a> and built a fort. Despite famine and disease, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jamestown">Jamestown</a> became the first permanent English settlement in America.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jamestown">Jamestown</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/virginia">Virginia</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1610">1610 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">416 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Henry IV of France is assassinated in Paris</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/francois-ravaillac">François Ravaillac</a> stabbed the king when his carriage was halted in the rue de la Ferronnerie. Henry, who had ended the Wars of Religion, was succeeded by his eight-year-old son Louis XIII.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1796">1796 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">230 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Edward Jenner performs the first vaccination</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Jenner inoculated eight-year-old James Phipps with cowpox and later showed the boy was immune to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/smallpox">smallpox</a>. Vaccination spread worldwide, and smallpox was declared eradicated in 1980.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1948">1948 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">78 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">David Ben-Gurion proclaims the State of Israel</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">As the British Mandate ended, Ben-Gurion declared Israel's independence in Tel Aviv. Neighbouring Arab states invaded the next day, and hundreds of thousands of Palestinians were displaced in the war.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1955">1955 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">71 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Soviet bloc signs the Warsaw Pact</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The USSR and seven Eastern European states formed a military alliance days after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/west-germany">West Germany</a> joined <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nato">NATO</a>. The pact lasted until 1991.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/warsaw">Warsaw</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1973">1973 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">53 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">NASA launches Skylab, America's first space station</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Skylab was launched on the last Saturn V flown. Damaged on ascent, it was repaired by its first crew, and three crews lived aboard for a total of 171 days.</p></div></li></ol>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-born"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-born">Born on 14 May <span class="n">5</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/victor-amadeus-ii"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/victor-amadeus-ii.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Victor Amadeus II</span><span class="tp">1666–1732</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/adolf-frederick-king-of-sweden"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/adolf-frederick-king-of-sweden.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Adolf Frederick, King of Sweden</span><span class="tp">1710–1771</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/ludovico-manin"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/ludovico-manin.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Ludovico Manin</span><span class="tp">1725–1802</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/kurt-eisner"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/kurt-eisner.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Kurt Eisner</span><span class="tp">1867–1919</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/ayub-khan"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/ayub-khan.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Ayub Khan</span><span class="tp">1907–1974</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-died"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-died">Died on 14 May <span class="n">7</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/william-marshal-1st-earl-of-pembroke"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/william-marshal-1st-earl-of-pembroke.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">William Marshal, 1st Earl of Pembroke</span><span class="tp">c. 1146–1219</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/tahmasp-i"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/tahmasp-i.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Tahmasp I</span><span class="tp">1514–1576</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/henry-iv-of-france"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/henry-iv-of-france.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Henry IV of France</span><span class="tp">1553–1610</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/louis-xiii-of-france"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/louis-xiii-of-france.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Louis XIII of France</span><span class="tp">1601–1643</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/okubo-toshimichi"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/okubo-toshimichi.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Okubo Toshimichi</span><span class="tp">1830–1878</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/willem-drees"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/willem-drees.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Willem Drees</span><span class="tp">1886–1988</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/jiang-qing"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/jiang-qing.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Jiang Qing</span><span class="tp">1914–1991</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<p class="day-ppl-note">Dates as the sources give them: in the Julian calendar before 1582, and in some countries for longer (Britain until 1752, Russia until 1918). Only people whose day of birth or death the records agree on are listed.</p>
